1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:17,243
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June eighth. This week, from the fourth to the tenth, is Japan's Dental and Oral Health Week. It's a yearly reminder to take good care of your teeth. Let's listen.

2
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:20,603
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:21,303 --> 00:00:28,047
[News] 6月4日から10日までは、「歯と口の健康週間」です。

4
00:00:28,748 --> 00:00:34,963
[News] これは、歯を大切にすることを考える1週間です。

5
00:00:35,664 --> 00:00:40,823
[News] 歯が痛いと、ごはんがおいしく食べられません。

6
00:00:41,524 --> 00:00:46,875
[News] だから、毎日歯をみがくことが大切です。

7
00:00:47,576 --> 00:00:52,783
[News] 朝と夜、特に寝る前にみがくといいです。

8
00:00:53,484 --> 00:00:58,740
[News] 歯みがきは、3分くらいかけてするといいです。

9
00:00:59,439 --> 00:01:03,807
[News] おくの歯も、わすれずにみがきましょう。

10
00:01:04,507 --> 00:01:09,475
[News] 甘いものを食べすぎないことも、大切です。

11
00:01:10,176 --> 00:01:14,855
[News] 食べたあとに、口をゆすぐのもいいです。

12
00:01:15,555 --> 00:01:21,123
[News] 子どもも大人も、ときどき歯医者さんに行きましょう。

13
00:01:21,823 --> 00:01:26,671
[News] 歯医者さんで、歯をきれいにしてもらえます。

14
00:01:27,371 --> 00:01:32,171
[News] 健康な歯は、一生の宝物です。

15
00:01:32,871 --> 00:01:37,623
[News] 元気な歯で、なんでもおいしく食べましょう。

16
00:01:38,323 --> 00:01:43,867
[News] 今週は、自分の歯について考えてみましょう。

17
00:01:44,567 --> 00:01:46,200
[Host] Let's break it down.

18
00:01:46,799 --> 00:01:54,504
[Slow] 6月4日から10日までは、「歯と口の健康週間」です。

19
00:01:55,304 --> 00:01:59,263
[Host] June fourth to the tenth is Dental and Oral Health Week.

20
00:01:59,864 --> 00:02:01,640
[Vocab] 歯

21
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:06,719
[Host] It means tooth, or teeth. You'll hear it in lots of health and food talk.

22
00:02:07,319 --> 00:02:13,223
[Slow] 歯が痛いと、ごはんがおいしく食べられません。

23
00:02:14,024 --> 00:02:17,072
[Host] When your teeth hurt, you can't enjoy your meals.

24
00:02:17,671 --> 00:02:19,831
[Vocab] 痛い

25
00:02:20,231 --> 00:02:26,039
[Host] It means painful, or it hurts. Use it for anything from a headache to a sore tooth.

26
00:02:26,639 --> 00:02:32,735
[Slow] だから、毎日歯をみがくことが大切です。

27
00:02:33,536 --> 00:02:37,592
[Host] So, brushing your teeth every day is important.

28
00:02:38,192 --> 00:02:40,472
[Vocab] みがく

29
00:02:40,872 --> 00:02:46,391
[Host] It means to brush, or to polish. You do it to your teeth, and to shoes too.

30
00:02:46,991 --> 00:02:52,943
[Slow] 朝と夜、特に寝る前にみがくといいです。

31
00:02:53,743 --> 00:02:58,111
[Host] Morning and night — especially before bed — it's good to brush.

32
00:02:58,711 --> 00:03:00,680
[Vocab] 寝る

33
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:06,264
[Host] It means to sleep, or to go to bed. Here it's the time just before sleeping.

34
00:03:06,864 --> 00:03:12,527
[Slow] 甘いものを食べすぎないことも、大切です。

35
00:03:13,328 --> 00:03:16,807
[Host] Not eating too many sweet things is also important.

36
00:03:17,407 --> 00:03:19,496
[Vocab] 甘い

37
00:03:19,895 --> 00:03:25,008
[Host] It means sweet. Great for candy, tough on your teeth in large amounts.

38
00:03:25,608 --> 00:03:31,967
[Slow] 子どもも大人も、ときどき歯医者さんに行きましょう。

39
00:03:32,768 --> 00:03:36,752
[Host] Children and adults alike should go to the dentist now and then.

40
00:03:37,352 --> 00:03:39,536
[Vocab] 歯医者

41
00:03:39,936 --> 00:03:43,367
[Host] It means dentist — literally the tooth doctor.

42
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:49,487
[Slow] 歯医者さんで、歯をきれいにしてもらえます。

43
00:03:50,288 --> 00:03:53,360
[Host] At the dentist, you can have your teeth cleaned.

44
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,975
[Vocab] きれい

45
00:03:56,376 --> 00:04:01,656
[Host] It means clean, and also pretty. Both senses are useful every day.

46
00:04:02,256 --> 00:04:07,752
[Slow] 健康な歯は、一生の宝物です。

47
00:04:08,551 --> 00:04:11,527
[Host] Healthy teeth are a treasure for your whole life.

48
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:14,503
[Vocab] 健康

49
00:04:14,903 --> 00:04:19,391
[Host] It means health, or healthy. The whole point of this special week.

50
00:04:19,992 --> 00:04:22,992
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

51
